@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why the agent's commits carry a resolved identity, and the precedence that resolves it
' covers: internal/gitidentity/gitidentity.go
'
' ── AN UNSET IDENTITY FAILS LATE AND BADLY ─────────────────────────────────
' A container has no git identity of its own. Without one the agent works
' normally, edits files, and then fails at the COMMIT with "Please tell me who you
' are" — after the work, not before it. On an unattended run that is a completed
' task with nothing recorded, which is the worst possible time to discover a
' missing two-line config.
'
' Resolve therefore runs host-side, before launch, and its result travels as env
' pairs the container cannot be missing.
'
' ── PRECEDENCE, AND WHY COMMITTER FALLS BACK ───────────────────────────────
' Environment first, then git config. Both are passed IN (getenv, gitConfig), so
' the resolution is testable without a git installation or a mutated environment.
'
' COMMITTER falls back to AUTHOR when only the author half is set. Git treats them
' as separate identities and will refuse on the missing one, so an operator who
' exported the pair they had heard of would still hit the late failure. The
' fallback makes the common half-configuration work rather than diagnosing it.
title internal/gitidentity — resolve before launch, not at the commit

participant "host env" as ENV <<data>>
participant "git config" as CFG <<data>>
participant "Resolve" as R <<app>>
participant "container" as C <<cloud>>

ENV ARROW_MAIN R : GIT_AUTHOR_* / GIT_COMMITTER_*
CFG ARROW_QUEUE R : fallback when env is silent
R ARROW_MAIN C : EnvPairs() — both identities, always set

note over R
  **Committer falls back to author.** Git refuses
  on whichever half is missing, so a half-set
  identity fails as completely as none — and only
  once the work is already done.
end note
@enduml
